.TH SYNC 2
.SH NAME
sync \- update super-block
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "sync( )"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sync
causes all information in core memory that should be on disk to be
written out.
This includes modified super blocks, modified i-nodes, and
delayed block I/O.
.PP
It should be used by programs which examine a file system, for example
.BR fsck (1),
.BR df (1),
etc.
A
.B sync
is done automatically when a program exits.
.SH BUGS
The writing, although scheduled, is not necessarily complete upon return
from
.BR sync .
.SH ASSEMBLER
(sync = 36.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys sync
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 36
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
